Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"216.200.128.254","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d4fdd08d0abbce9890dcc47f543d5ffc","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:18px;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update 1.7.2015&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I can&#039;t believe it&#039;s already January! &amp;nbsp;66 days to go, eek!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beauty Salon Stuff - Hair Extensions, Dye, Lash Extensions, Tanning, oh my!&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I went in today for my extension consultation! &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m going to get a \"Halo\" hair extension, so I can reuse it and not damage by the water. &amp;nbsp;She recommended not doing a semi-permanent type because I&#039;m going to be in the water a LOT, and even the beaded ones you&#039;re not supposed to get submerged, etc. &amp;nbsp;This way I can do it myself when I want, like for the rehearsal dinner, and then the day of the wedding the salon can style it into my hair! &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m going to try to go with as much down as possible, probably long to the side - very similar to what @[member=\"tygrrlily\"] did, actually :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;ve decided I&#039;m going to get my hair dyed ombre (from my natural dark brown on the top to a lighter brown\/dark blonde on the tips) too. &amp;nbsp;Why not? :) &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m going to get it done 2 weeks before I leave, so it leaves time to change it if I need to. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;ll also give them time to dye the extensions to match (they can dye it to my natural brown back after the wedding, once I decide I&#039;m done with my hair that way!)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m also going to do the lash extensions 3-4 weeks before I go, and get them filled the week before. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m going to start with the more natural, and if I feel I want more, I&#039;ll get the luxury ones.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;And I remembered that I am pretty white, and PROBABLY should start tanning...so they were running a 2015 special for 20.15 per month (usually they charge 40), and that takes me to right before I go. &amp;nbsp;So I started working on my base today. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m not going for dark, more a base so I&#039;m less likely to burn and have a little color :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m pretty excited, but beauty is EXPENSIVE!! &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s a once in a lifetime thing, and since I don&#039;t go to the salon hardly ever, I&#039;m thinking of it as all at once versus spread out over the year haha.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TTD dress&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I picked this up and tried it on while I was in Chicago for the holidays - I think it&#039;ll be perfect for the TTD session! &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s very light and flowy, and I think it&#039;ll look pretty awesome underwater. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s a *little* bit small in the bust area, but I have 2 months so it&#039;ll fit :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79656]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79657]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TTD shoes&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;So I worked on my \"mermaid shoes\" (as my 3 year old calls them!) over the weekend. &amp;nbsp;I was told not to wear heels during the ceremony on the beach, and I wear flipflops unless it&#039;s snowy\/icy year round anyway, so I didn&#039;t see the need to change to heels for the reception. &amp;nbsp;But I loved a few TTD shots of I believe they were red heels, and knew I wanted some to take with us for that! &amp;nbsp;So I looked online and couldn&#039;t find any that I loved, and so I decided to DIY. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;I chose to use a pair of heels I already had, that were kinda scuffed. &amp;nbsp;Love them - Chinese laundry, and have leather uppers. &amp;nbsp;I wanted something unique (not just pumps).&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;I followed this tutorial more or less:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.ateaspoonofhappiness.com\/diy-glitter-shoes\/&#039;&gt;http:\/\/www.ateaspoonofhappiness.com\/diy-glitter-shoes\/&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;My supplies&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79651]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;Wet glue in the front, drying glue in the back (I have to admit, I was a little scared before they started to dry...)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79652]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;These pictures REALLY don&#039;t do them justice. &amp;nbsp;They are BEAUTIFUL and VERY sparkly!&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79653]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79654]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79655]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;I am working on the underside now - I&#039;m trying to do white glitter with the \"I do\" stickers. &amp;nbsp;If you&#039;re going to do this, remember to do FINE glitter, not chunky. &amp;nbsp;I had some chunky silver and thought \"Hey that would look cool underneath and I don&#039;t have to buy more glitter!\". &amp;nbsp;Yah. &amp;nbsp;2 hours of chiseling the clumpy awfulness later...ha. &amp;nbsp;And white glitter isn&#039;t actually all white...it&#039;s actually a blue green. &amp;nbsp;Weird, I know. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ll post more pictures when they are completely dry &amp;amp; I have the stickers on! &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m going to seal them too, since I&#039;m using them underwater&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bouquets&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;Finally finished! &amp;nbsp;I had to order &amp;amp; make a 4th bouquet, since my FSIL is now on FI side (same color), so that&#039;s why there are 2 of the same color ribbon. &amp;nbsp;The liles that came are actually a little different than the other 3, so I decided she&#039;s going to have a slightly different one. &amp;nbsp;I don&#039;t really care at this point, hahaha. &amp;nbsp;The roses &amp;amp; three color ribbon is my tossing bouquet for the bouquet toss - turned out pretty cute :)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79637]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79639]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Groomsmen Shirts&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Finally got the FI to pick out shirts. &amp;nbsp;He&#039;s going to be in a white shirt with the white paisley bow ties, and then the other three groomsmen (well, 2 groomsmen and 1 groomsmaid) will match the bridesmaids. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Best man shirt (lavender) and similar color bowtie (raspberry) - my dad will have the same color shirt and a long necktie in the same color:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79643]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;3rd groomsman shirt (some blue...) and similar color bowtie (malibu) - his dad will have this combo only a necktie:&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79642]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Centerpieces&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;Put together the centerpieces at my MILs house, and I think we&#039;re good to go! &amp;nbsp;I got orchids from walmart on a $5 stem, and pulled them off for the centerpieces. &amp;nbsp;I was going to hot glue them in, but we decided to test them without. &amp;nbsp;I was pleasantly surprised - they actually floated and feel like realistic flowers once wet. &amp;nbsp;And it looked great! &amp;nbsp;We also decided to add a bit of glass to the bottom of the bowls in dark blue\/teal\/clear, and it looked great. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;I plan on using a circle mirror (instead of a microwave plate haha) on the bottom to help reflect the light. &amp;nbsp;I can&#039;t wait to see them in the dark! &amp;nbsp;I made 4 tables worth, which with the guests we have now, we&#039;ll have 3 tables of 9 or 4 tables of 7. &amp;nbsp;If any more guests book, I&#039;ll for sure go for 4 tables. &amp;nbsp;We&#039;re doing a sweetheart table for the two of us, and I can always do a different centerpiece (or pay for one of theirs so I don&#039;t have to worry about it!)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79649]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79650]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DIY Ringbearer Box&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m so excited about this! &amp;nbsp;I think it turned out pretty cute. &amp;nbsp;My MIL had some colored felt, and this was close to the lighter blue color in the wedding, and I had leftover royal blue ribbon. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ll trim the ribbons back the day of, when we take pictures with the rings in the box. &amp;nbsp;I don&#039;t want to trim it until we have both sets of rings. &amp;nbsp;My FIL is going to stain the middle piece and glue it in, so it&#039;s flush. &amp;nbsp;And I used my FSIL&#039;s engagement ring for the 2nd ring, haha, for demonstration purposes. &amp;nbsp;I love it!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Gluing in the letters&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79644]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;The \"guts\" of the pillow&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79645]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;Outside of the box (which I&#039;m still in love with!)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79646]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79647]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;With the rings in there :)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79648]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;That&#039;s most of my updates for now - working on the Vistaprint order and some of the other printables. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ve also packed the OOT bags outside of the chapstick, as FI still hasn&#039;t reprinted the labels. &amp;nbsp;A productive week so far!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1882171,"PostDate":1420661427,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><span  style=\"font-size:18px\"><strong>Update 1.7.2015<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I can't believe it's already January! \u00a066 days to go, eek!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Beauty Salon Stuff - Hair Extensions, Dye, Lash Extensions, Tanning, oh my!<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>I went in today for my extension consultation! \u00a0I'm going to get a \"Halo\" hair extension, so I can reuse it and not damage by the water. \u00a0She recommended not doing a semi-permanent type because I'm going to be in the water a LOT, and even the beaded ones you're not supposed to get submerged, etc. \u00a0This way I can do it myself when I want, like for the rehearsal dinner, and then the day of the wedding the salon can style it into my hair! \u00a0I'm going to try to go with as much down as possible, probably long to the side - very similar to what @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277296\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277296-tygrrlily\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">tygrrlily<\/span><\/a> did, actually <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I've decided I'm going to get my hair dyed ombre (from my natural dark brown on the top to a lighter brown\/dark blonde on the tips) too. \u00a0Why not? <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0I'm going to get it done 2 weeks before I leave, so it leaves time to change it if I need to. \u00a0It'll also give them time to dye the extensions to match (they can dye it to my natural brown back after the wedding, once I decide I'm done with my hair that way!)<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm also going to do the lash extensions 3-4 weeks before I go, and get them filled the week before. \u00a0I'm going to start with the more natural, and if I feel I want more, I'll get the luxury ones.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>And I remembered that I am pretty white, and PROBABLY should start tanning...so they were running a 2015 special for 20.15 per month (usually they charge 40), and that takes me to right before I go. \u00a0So I started working on my base today. \u00a0I'm not going for dark, more a base so I'm less likely to burn and have a little color <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm pretty excited, but beauty is EXPENSIVE!! \u00a0It's a once in a lifetime thing, and since I don't go to the salon hardly ever, I'm thinking of it as all at once versus spread out over the year haha.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>TTD dress<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>I picked this up and tried it on while I was in Chicago for the holidays - I think it'll be perfect for the TTD session! \u00a0It's very light and flowy, and I think it'll look pretty awesome underwater. \u00a0It's a *little* bit small in the bust area, but I have 2 months so it'll fit <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79656-ttd-dress-jordan-455-bridesmaid-dress-in-white\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_2027391.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='TTD dress (Jordan 455, bridesmaid dress in white)'  width='150' height='200'  alt='TTD dress (Jordan 455, bridesmaid dress in white)' id='sml_image_view_79656' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79657-ttd-dress-jordan-455-bridesmaid-dress-in-white\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1248231.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='TTD dress (Jordan 455, bridesmaid dress in white)'  width='150' height='200'  alt='TTD dress (Jordan 455, bridesmaid dress in white)' id='sml_image_view_79657' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><strong>TTD shoes<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>So I worked on my \"mermaid shoes\" (as my 3 year old calls them!) over the weekend. \u00a0I was told not to wear heels during the ceremony on the beach, and I wear flipflops unless it's snowy\/icy year round anyway, so I didn't see the need to change to heels for the reception. \u00a0But I loved a few TTD shots of I believe they were red heels, and knew I wanted some to take with us for that! \u00a0So I looked online and couldn't find any that I loved, and so I decided to DIY. \u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I chose to use a pair of heels I already had, that were kinda scuffed. \u00a0Love them - Chinese laundry, and have leather uppers. \u00a0I wanted something unique (not just pumps).<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I followed this tutorial more or less:\u00a0<a href='http:\/\/www.ateaspoonofhappiness.com\/diy-glitter-shoes\/' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.ateaspoon...-glitter-shoes\/<\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>My supplies<\/div>\n<div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79651-glitter-ttd-shoes\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1065728.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='glitter TTD shoes'  width='200' height='150'  alt='glitter TTD shoes' id='sml_image_view_79651' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Wet glue in the front, drying glue in the back (I have to admit, I was a little scared before they started to dry...)<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79652-glitter-ttd-shoes\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_2033484.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='glitter TTD shoes'  width='150' height='200'  alt='glitter TTD shoes' id='sml_image_view_79652' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>These pictures REALLY don't do them justice. \u00a0They are BEAUTIFUL and VERY sparkly!<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79653-glitter-ttd-shoes\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_418519.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='glitter TTD shoes'  width='150' height='200'  alt='glitter TTD shoes' id='sml_image_view_79653' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79654-glitter-ttd-shoes\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_180393.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='glitter TTD shoes'  width='150' height='200'  alt='glitter TTD shoes' id='sml_image_view_79654' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79655-glitter-ttd-shoes\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1167517.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='glitter TTD shoes'  width='150' height='200'  alt='glitter TTD shoes' id='sml_image_view_79655' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I am working on the underside now - I'm trying to do white glitter with the \"I do\" stickers. \u00a0If you're going to do this, remember to do FINE glitter, not chunky. \u00a0I had some chunky silver and thought \"Hey that would look cool underneath and I don't have to buy more glitter!\". \u00a0Yah. \u00a02 hours of chiseling the clumpy awfulness later...ha. \u00a0And white glitter isn't actually all white...it's actually a blue green. \u00a0Weird, I know. \u00a0I'll post more pictures when they are completely dry & I have the stickers on! \u00a0I'm going to seal them too, since I'm using them underwater<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><strong>Bouquets<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>Finally finished! \u00a0I had to order & make a 4th bouquet, since my FSIL is now on FI side (same color), so that's why there are 2 of the same color ribbon. \u00a0The liles that came are actually a little different than the other 3, so I decided she's going to have a slightly different one. \u00a0I don't really care at this point, hahaha. \u00a0The roses & three color ribbon is my tossing bouquet for the bouquet toss - turned out pretty cute <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79637-bridesmaid-bouquets-groomsmaid\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_2156979.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='bridesmaid bouquets (+ groomsmaid)'  width='200' height='150'  alt='bridesmaid bouquets (+ groomsmaid)' id='sml_image_view_79637' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79639-tossing-bouquet\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_2697790.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='tossing bouquet'  width='150' height='200'  alt='tossing bouquet' id='sml_image_view_79639' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Groomsmen Shirts<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Finally got the FI to pick out shirts. \u00a0He's going to be in a white shirt with the white paisley bow ties, and then the other three groomsmen (well, 2 groomsmen and 1 groomsmaid) will match the bridesmaids. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Best man shirt (lavender) and similar color bowtie (raspberry) - my dad will have the same color shirt and a long necktie in the same color:<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79643-groomsman-shirt-tie\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_682031.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='groomsman shirt & tie'  width='150' height='200'  alt='groomsman shirt & tie' id='sml_image_view_79643' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>3rd groomsman shirt (some blue...) and similar color bowtie (malibu) - his dad will have this combo only a necktie:<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79642-groomsman-shirt-tie\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_3672772.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='groomsman shirt & tie'  width='150' height='200'  alt='groomsman shirt & tie' id='sml_image_view_79642' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><strong>Centerpieces<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>Put together the centerpieces at my MILs house, and I think we're good to go! \u00a0I got orchids from walmart on a $5 stem, and pulled them off for the centerpieces. \u00a0I was going to hot glue them in, but we decided to test them without. \u00a0I was pleasantly surprised - they actually floated and feel like realistic flowers once wet. \u00a0And it looked great! \u00a0We also decided to add a bit of glass to the bottom of the bowls in dark blue\/teal\/clear, and it looked great. \u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I plan on using a circle mirror (instead of a microwave plate haha) on the bottom to help reflect the light. \u00a0I can't wait to see them in the dark! \u00a0I made 4 tables worth, which with the guests we have now, we'll have 3 tables of 9 or 4 tables of 7. \u00a0If any more guests book, I'll for sure go for 4 tables. \u00a0We're doing a sweetheart table for the two of us, and I can always do a different centerpiece (or pay for one of theirs so I don't have to worry about it!)<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79649-centerpiece-trial-with-water\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_502423.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='centerpiece trial with water'  width='150' height='200'  alt='centerpiece trial with water' id='sml_image_view_79649' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79650-centerpiece-trial-with-water\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1100031.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='centerpiece trial with water'  width='150' height='200'  alt='centerpiece trial with water' id='sml_image_view_79650' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>DIY Ringbearer Box<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>I'm so excited about this! \u00a0I think it turned out pretty cute. \u00a0My MIL had some colored felt, and this was close to the lighter blue color in the wedding, and I had leftover royal blue ribbon. \u00a0I'll trim the ribbons back the day of, when we take pictures with the rings in the box. \u00a0I don't want to trim it until we have both sets of rings. \u00a0My FIL is going to stain the middle piece and glue it in, so it's flush. \u00a0And I used my FSIL's engagement ring for the 2nd ring, haha, for demonstration purposes. \u00a0I love it!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Gluing in the letters<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79644-ring-bearer-box\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1844189.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='ring bearer box'  width='150' height='200'  alt='ring bearer box' id='sml_image_view_79644' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>The \"guts\" of the pillow<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79645-ring-bearer-box\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1682050.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='ring bearer box'  width='150' height='200'  alt='ring bearer box' id='sml_image_view_79645' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Outside of the box (which I'm still in love with!)<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79646-ring-bearer-box\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_2405541.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='ring bearer box'  width='150' height='200'  alt='ring bearer box' id='sml_image_view_79646' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79647-ring-bearer-box\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_547281.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='ring bearer box'  width='150' height='200'  alt='ring bearer box' id='sml_image_view_79647' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>With the rings in there <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79648-ring-bearer-box\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_280838.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='ring bearer box'  width='150' height='200'  alt='ring bearer box' id='sml_image_view_79648' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That's most of my updates for now - working on the Vistaprint order and some of the other printables. \u00a0I've also packed the OOT bags outside of the chapstick, as FI still hasn't reprinted the labels. \u00a0A productive week so far!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"32 guests, Bride & Groom & 2 kids booked!Planning Thread - lots of pictures, DIY\/templates and ongoing updates!<br><br><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/<\/span><\/a>","Email":"marinarhianne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.149.51.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1387570652,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275696.jpeg?_r=1426773379","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"marinah84","Id":275696,"Name":"marinah84","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"235d0c62639cece036025820dba3ae55","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Awesome! everything looks great and is coming together!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You are crafty with those shoes - they look fantastic - I would never be daring enough. Well maybe, but they would never look that good!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I got my hair died 1.5 weeks before we leave, I just don&#039;t have time to do it next week. I am ok with it, the growth won&#039;t be overly bad - if even noticable at all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I started to tan, but since I have minutes at the gym I find I only tan when I work out and honestly, just not much time for that lately or I go to a different gym depending on their class schedule. &amp;nbsp;Sigh, kind of late now, maybe I will try to go 2-3 more times.   &lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Sounds like things are coming along!!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1882184,"PostDate":1420663981,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Awesome! everything looks great and is coming together!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You are crafty with those shoes - they look fantastic - I would never be daring enough. Well maybe, but they would never look that good!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I got my hair died 1.5 weeks before we leave, I just don't have time to do it next week. I am ok with it, the growth won't be overly bad - if even noticable at all.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I started to tan, but since I have minutes at the gym I find I only tan when I work out and honestly, just not much time for that lately or I go to a different gym depending on their class schedule. \u00a0Sigh, kind of late now, maybe I will try to go 2-3 more times. \u00a0\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Sounds like things are coming along!!!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"216.200.128.254","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d4e6b37847f265af3c8f51e8980630f2","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] &amp;nbsp;I go to a small crossfit gym, so I don&#039;t have a tanning bed there! &amp;nbsp;There are only a few gyms in town, and none have lap pools, so I decided to go with a class-type gym that will motivate me to go more. &amp;nbsp;I love it! &amp;nbsp;My gym is VERY safe, everything is safety-conscious, so it&#039;s not like those garage boxes you see on Crossfit fail youtube videos haha. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m a very strong girl, and competitive, so it&#039;s been great for me!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;FI may actually tan for the first time in his life, and he&#039;s talking about joining a gym so he can run and tan (he&#039;s got a marathon in April and our treadmill is being wonky). &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ll believe it when I see it ;)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;What are you packing as \"emergency\" items, Kim? &amp;nbsp;I already have on my list to bring a glue gun, since I have so much DIY stuff (like the bouts) that I am worried they might fall apart lol. &amp;nbsp;Anything else you&#039;re packing? &amp;nbsp;Or anything anyone else has brought they found useful?&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1882205,"PostDate":1420712226,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> \u00a0I go to a small crossfit gym, so I don't have a tanning bed there! \u00a0There are only a few gyms in town, and none have lap pools, so I decided to go with a class-type gym that will motivate me to go more. \u00a0I love it! \u00a0My gym is VERY safe, everything is safety-conscious, so it's not like those garage boxes you see on Crossfit fail youtube videos haha. \u00a0I'm a very strong girl, and competitive, so it's been great for me!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>FI may actually tan for the first time in his life, and he's talking about joining a gym so he can run and tan (he's got a marathon in April and our treadmill is being wonky). \u00a0I'll believe it when I see it <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>What are you packing as \"emergency\" items, Kim? \u00a0I already have on my list to bring a glue gun, since I have so much DIY stuff (like the bouts) that I am worried they might fall apart lol. \u00a0Anything else you're packing? \u00a0Or anything anyone else has brought they found useful?<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"32 guests, Bride & Groom & 2 kids booked!Planning Thread - lots of pictures, DIY\/templates and ongoing updates!<br><br><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/<\/span><\/a>","Email":"marinarhianne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.149.51.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1387570652,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275696.jpeg?_r=1426773379","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"marinah84","Id":275696,"Name":"marinah84","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1420713564,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d6bce6236a4f605d05f249114ab098af","RawContent":"[quote name=\"marinah84\" post=\"1882205\" timestamp=\"1420726626\"]\n@[member=\"calgarybride2015\"]  I go to a small crossfit gym, so I don&#039;t have a tanning bed there!  There are only a few gyms in town, and none have lap pools, so I decided to go with a class-type gym that will motivate me to go more.  I love it!  My gym is VERY safe, everything is safety-conscious, so it&#039;s not like those garage boxes you see on Crossfit fail youtube videos haha.  I&#039;m a very strong girl, and competitive, so it&#039;s been great for me!\n\nFI may actually tan for the first time in his life, and he&#039;s talking about joining a gym so he can run and tan (he&#039;s got a marathon in April and our treadmill is being wonky).  I&#039;ll believe it when I see it ;)\n\n\nWhat are you packing as \"emergency\" items, Kim?  I already have on my list to bring a glue gun, since I have so much DIY stuff (like the bouts) that I am worried they might fall apart lol.  Anything else you&#039;re packing?  Or anything anyone else has brought they found useful?[\/quote]\n\nI believe you with the comment &#039;I&#039;ll believe it when I see it&#039;  Shawn joined the gym in September and maybe has went 4-5x, maybe!!!   He was going to tan too but hasn&#039;t went so here we are 9 (yes 9) days from leaving and we are slackers!   I would have thought this would be the time I am in the best shape of my life and alas I am not hahahah!!  dress fits so I am happy!\n\nI would love to hear what past brides forgot and wish they had - or the best thing they brought.\n\nI plan to bring glue gun, extra ribbon, scissors, sewing kit, travel steamer, humidity spray (just bought, yay!), clothing tape, blotting clothes for my face, every med known to man for myself\/my kids.    I also just realized my kids didn&#039;t have real sun hats, only ball caps, so thankfully I found some yesterday at Osk Kosh.   I got them crocs as water shoes so they are dual purpose if they need water shoes,I also got them long sleeve SPF\/rash guard shirts, I also was told to get the sunscreen stick for their faces.  hmmmmm I am sure there is more but drawing a blank at this moment. \n\nThe sunscreen for the 4 of us may take up half the suitcase lol","Attachments":[],"Id":1882206,"PostDate":1420713494,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>marinah84, on 08 January 2015 - 10:17 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> \u00a0I go to a small crossfit gym, so I don't have a tanning bed there! \u00a0There are only a few gyms in town, and none have lap pools, so I decided to go with a class-type gym that will motivate me to go more. \u00a0I love it! \u00a0My gym is VERY safe, everything is safety-conscious, so it's not like those garage boxes you see on Crossfit fail youtube videos haha. \u00a0I'm a very strong girl, and competitive, so it's been great for me!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>FI may actually tan for the first time in his life, and he's talking about joining a gym so he can run and tan (he's got a marathon in April and our treadmill is being wonky). \u00a0I'll believe it when I see it <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>What are you packing as \"emergency\" items, Kim? \u00a0I already have on my list to bring a glue gun, since I have so much DIY stuff (like the bouts) that I am worried they might fall apart lol. \u00a0Anything else you're packing? \u00a0Or anything anyone else has brought they found useful?<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I believe you with the comment 'I'll believe it when I see it' \u00a0Shawn joined the gym in September and maybe has went 4-5x, maybe!!! \u00a0 He was going to tan too but hasn't went so here we are 9 (yes 9) days from leaving and we are slackers! \u00a0 I would have thought this would be the time I am in the best shape of my life and alas I am not hahahah!! \u00a0dress fits so I am happy!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I would love to hear what past brides forgot and wish they had - or the best thing they brought.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I plan to bring glue gun, extra ribbon, scissors, sewing kit, travel steamer, humidity spray (just bought, yay!), clothing tape, blotting clothes for my face, every med known to man for myself\/my kids. \u00a0 \u00a0I also just realized my kids didn't have real sun hats, only ball caps, so thankfully I found some yesterday at Osk Kosh. \u00a0 I got them crocs as water shoes so they are dual purpose if they need water shoes,I also got them long sleeve SPF\/rash guard shirts, I also was told to get the sunscreen stick for their faces. \u00a0hmmmmm I am sure there is more but drawing a blank at this moment.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The sunscreen for the 4 of us may take up half the suitcase lol<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"216.200.128.254","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"22861fb53950b1879aa3094809da6a00","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:18px;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update 1.12.2015&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Small update today! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ring Bearer Gifts&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;My son is young and I wanted to do something that he can keep from the wedding, and something for him to DO during the reception. &amp;nbsp;There really aren&#039;t a lot of cute options for ring bearers - same with boys clothes, compared to girls, so it&#039;s par for the course I guess!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Keep - I got this off of Etsy, from this shop:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/www.etsy.com\/shop\/JustForYouEngravings&#039;&gt;https:\/\/www.etsy.com\/shop\/JustForYouEngravings&lt;\/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;It was very well constructed, and came really fast! &amp;nbsp;I don&#039;t know if he&#039;ll like baseball when he&#039;s bigger, but the way he loves to throw around balls now, I&#039;m sure he&#039;ll appreciate the gift. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s going on his shelf in his room :) &lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79659]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Wear - I got this off of ebay. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s nice, came in 2T (my son is a TANK) and fast shipping! &amp;nbsp;She&#039;s currently \"away\" at her store on vacation, but has amazing feedback from the last 12 months. &amp;nbsp;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.ebay.com\/usr\/babyrocks867?rt=nc&#039;&gt;http:\/\/www.ebay.com\/usr\/babyrocks867?rt=nc&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79677]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Do:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m planning on getting some glowsticks and small toys in an activity bag for him for the reception. &amp;nbsp;I figure he&#039;s only going to be good until about 8pm at the latest (due to bedtime and the heat) so I don&#039;t think it&#039;ll need to be much. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ll print him out a coloring book like his sister, but he&#039;s not overly interested so far. &amp;nbsp;I figure the food will take up a lot of his attention haha. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m going to get him some sand toys\/etc as well as something with wheels since he loves cars (and sports balls, but I don&#039;t want him throwing it at me in the middle of the reception lol!)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cake&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;It looks like we won&#039;t make the 20 rooms booked (we&#039;ll be somewhere between 17-19, drat) for some of the more free items on the packages, drat. &amp;nbsp;So we&#039;ll have to buy our cake. &amp;nbsp;This is the cake we chose - they are going to do the pink gerber (sp?) daisies the same and add in blue roses. &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s only $40 for 30 people, yay! &amp;nbsp;The other items on the package honestly weren&#039;t a great deal anyway - it&#039;s 35 rooms booked where you get hair done\/3 bottles of champagne\/late checkout\/room upgrade\/etc. &amp;nbsp;We still hit the 15 for the min basic package to be free, so we&#039;re happy! &amp;nbsp;Also - our dinner includes dessert as well...so we didn&#039;t need a big cake anyway!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79675]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shake for a Kiss Maracas Tags&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So we will need to go out to the markets to get tequila for our tequila toast (supposedly...which is weird, since it&#039;s an all inclusive! &amp;nbsp;not doing straight shots of liquor, so again a little weird) so while we&#039;re out, was planning on finding a street vendor with maracas that we can get for about $1\/person. &amp;nbsp;That&#039;s how much they were without haggling in both Cozumel &amp;amp; Cabo so crossing fingers it&#039;s similar or we can haggle them down since we&#039;ll buy around 30!).&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I made these tags based on a poem I found on the forum, and will print\/cut them to bring. &amp;nbsp;If we don&#039;t use them, oh well! &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m out some paper &amp;amp; ink. &amp;nbsp;I used an Avery tags template and will just print them on regular paper\/cardstock I already have. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79676]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What I&#039;m currently working on - Printables!:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Kids Coloring Book (I&#039;m doing it from scratch...we&#039;ll see how it goes!)&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Menu\/I Spy Rack Card (Vistaprint)&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Program Oversized Postcard (Vistaprint) - done, just need to order&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Wedding Timeline Postcard (Vistaprint) - debating putting something on the back with our wedding photo app\/instagram&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Door Knockers (Vistaprint) - possibly, still up in the air. &amp;nbsp;Depends on costs, and a little worried based on posts of rooms getting broken into...&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;\/ul&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1882672,"PostDate":1421089601,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><span  style=\"font-size:18px\"><strong>Update 1.12.2015<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Small update today! \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Ring Bearer Gifts<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>My son is young and I wanted to do something that he can keep from the wedding, and something for him to DO during the reception. \u00a0There really aren't a lot of cute options for ring bearers - same with boys clothes, compared to girls, so it's par for the course I guess!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Keep - I got this off of Etsy, from this shop:\u00a0<a href='https:\/\/www.etsy.com\/shop\/JustForYouEngravings' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>https:\/\/www.etsy.com...orYouEngravings<\/a>. \u00a0It was very well constructed, and came really fast! \u00a0I don't know if he'll like baseball when he's bigger, but the way he loves to throw around balls now, I'm sure he'll appreciate the gift. \u00a0It's going on his shelf in his room <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> <\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79659-ring-bearer-gift\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_2516328.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='ring bearer gift'  width='150' height='200'  alt='ring bearer gift' id='sml_image_view_79659' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wear - I got this off of ebay. \u00a0It's nice, came in 2T (my son is a TANK) and fast shipping! \u00a0She's currently \"away\" at her store on vacation, but has amazing feedback from the last 12 months. \u00a0<a href='http:\/\/www.ebay.com\/usr\/babyrocks867?rt=nc' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.ebay.com\/...yrocks867?rt=nc<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79677-ring-bearer-gift\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_2360593.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Ring bearer gift'  width='150' height='200'  alt='Ring bearer gift' id='sml_image_view_79677' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>Do:<\/p>\n<p>I'm planning on getting some glowsticks and small toys in an activity bag for him for the reception. \u00a0I figure he's only going to be good until about 8pm at the latest (due to bedtime and the heat) so I don't think it'll need to be much. \u00a0I'll print him out a coloring book like his sister, but he's not overly interested so far. \u00a0I figure the food will take up a lot of his attention haha. \u00a0I'm going to get him some sand toys\/etc as well as something with wheels since he loves cars (and sports balls, but I don't want him throwing it at me in the middle of the reception lol!)<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Cake<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It looks like we won't make the 20 rooms booked (we'll be somewhere between 17-19, drat) for some of the more free items on the packages, drat. \u00a0So we'll have to buy our cake. \u00a0This is the cake we chose - they are going to do the pink gerber (sp?) daisies the same and add in blue roses. \u00a0It's only $40 for 30 people, yay! \u00a0The other items on the package honestly weren't a great deal anyway - it's 35 rooms booked where you get hair done\/3 bottles of champagne\/late checkout\/room upgrade\/etc. \u00a0We still hit the 15 for the min basic package to be free, so we're happy! \u00a0Also - our dinner includes dessert as well...so we didn't need a big cake anyway!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79675-cake\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_49926.png' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='cake'  width='200' height='175'  alt='cake' id='sml_image_view_79675' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Shake for a Kiss Maracas Tags<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>So we will need to go out to the markets to get tequila for our tequila toast (supposedly...which is weird, since it's an all inclusive! \u00a0not doing straight shots of liquor, so again a little weird) so while we're out, was planning on finding a street vendor with maracas that we can get for about $1\/person. \u00a0That's how much they were without haggling in both Cozumel & Cabo so crossing fingers it's similar or we can haggle them down since we'll buy around 30!).<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I made these tags based on a poem I found on the forum, and will print\/cut them to bring. \u00a0If we don't use them, oh well! \u00a0I'm out some paper & ink. \u00a0I used an Avery tags template and will just print them on regular paper\/cardstock I already have. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79676-maracas-tags\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_83738.png' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Maracas Tags'  width='200' height='141'  alt='Maracas Tags' id='sml_image_view_79676' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>What I'm currently working on - Printables!:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul><li>Kids Coloring Book (I'm doing it from scratch...we'll see how it goes!)<\/li>\n<li>Menu\/I Spy Rack Card (Vistaprint)<\/li>\n<li>Program Oversized Postcard (Vistaprint) - done, just need to order<\/li>\n<li>Wedding Timeline Postcard (Vistaprint) - debating putting something on the back with our wedding photo app\/instagram<\/li>\n<li>Door Knockers (Vistaprint) - possibly, still up in the air. \u00a0Depends on costs, and a little worried based on posts of rooms getting broken into...<\/li>\n<\/ul>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"32 guests, Bride & Groom & 2 kids booked!Planning Thread - lots of pictures, DIY\/templates and ongoing updates!<br><br><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/<\/span><\/a>","Email":"marinarhianne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.149.51.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1387570652,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275696.jpeg?_r=1426773379","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"marinah84","Id":275696,"Name":"marinah84","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.151.178.186","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f5526712ea17652a781bad2b3cd80af3","RawContent":"Wow! You should go into business! everything is awesome! Kim is right - you&#039;re so crafty!!! It&#039;s the area where I fail. Dismally. Could you post your tags once you have it printed? I&#039;m trying to do the same thing but a different design and different saying but I&#039;ve redesigned the tag 3 times and have hated it every single time. Like I said - a dismal failure when it comes to DIY. Thank goodness we&#039;re already married!!","Attachments":[],"Id":1882675,"PostDate":1421092889,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Wow! You should go into business! everything is awesome! Kim is right - you're so crafty!!! It's the area where I fail. Dismally. Could you post your tags once you have it printed? I'm trying to do the same thing but a different design and different saying but I've redesigned the tag 3 times and have hated it every single time. Like I said - a dismal failure when it comes to DIY. Thank goodness we're already married!!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283444599,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1426134867","PhotoWidth":668,"PhotoHeight":600,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d906eb206eb472f988293818bc1e1ea9","RawContent":"Awesome!!! Love it all and cakes similiar to mine :) \n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1882685,"PostDate":1421095755,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Awesome!!! Love it all and cakes similiar to mine <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"216.200.128.254","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1421148066,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"599d3ba2d515450751cae0ddf3ebb612","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:18px;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update 1.13.2015&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I am working on printables today, and here are a few templates.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wedding Day Timeline Card&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The wedding day timeline I pretty much straight up used someone elses on here (I can&#039;t find her thread right now, whoops) and just changed the times\/what it said. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m planning on changing the fonts on my personal computer (I can&#039;t download fonts to my work computer). I&#039;m planning on printing these via Vistaprint on the regular or 4x6 postcards. &amp;nbsp;Probably will include our instagram tag &amp;amp; wedding day photo site information on the back (is it worth $5 to print? probably, then I don&#039;t have to do it elsewhere like business cards...). &amp;nbsp;These are going in the OOT bags.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79711]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Menu\/Photo Scavenger Hunt&lt;\/b&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;ve also included my menu front &amp;amp; back with photo scavenger hunt. &amp;nbsp;I again used the words from another person for the photo scavenger hunt, although I did customize the shots to capture. &amp;nbsp;These I will print on rack cards and have places on the plates at the reception. &amp;nbsp;I think this is the menu we&#039;re going to go with; I was trying to find things that everyone would like, or at least most everyone. &amp;nbsp;Still debating, and will have FI have final say (he was verbally on board, and suggested the Chef Salad instead of Caesar as well as the Minestrone soup, and agreed on the reasons behind the dessert being a brownie &amp;amp; ice cream, especially with cake already!)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79712]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:79713]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m working through my wedding day timeline, and deciding if I want to go with Styling Trio for my hair\/makeup or the salon. &amp;nbsp;I requested a quote, and got a bunch of social media information (which I had already found!) but no pricing. &amp;nbsp;The salon pricing isn&#039;t terrible - it&#039;s $50\/bridesmaid &amp;amp; $220ish for me for hair\/hair trial\/makeup (if I pay up front). &amp;nbsp;I don&#039;t have any examples of their work though, and that worries me...I am considering doing a mixture of both salon &amp;amp; styling trio. &amp;nbsp;Or all of one\/the other. &amp;nbsp;I need them to respond with pricing though, haha!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Does this seem a reasonable timeline for a 4pm wedding? &amp;nbsp;I have Samuel Luna from 230-830pm (photographer).&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;9:00 am \u2013 Nails&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;11:00 am \u2013 Room Service Lunch (ladies)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;12:00 pm \u2013 Hair &amp;amp; Makeup&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;2:30 pm - Photos of Groom and Groomsman getting ready&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;3:00 pm - Photos of Bride and Bridesmaids getting ready&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;3:45 pm - Guests arrive at wedding ceremony site&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;4:00 pm - Wedding Ceremony&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;4:30 pm - Tequila Shot Toast&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;4:45 pm \u2013 Group Photos&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;5:00 pm - Family Photos and Informal Cocktail Hour (Lobby Bar)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;5:15 pm - Bride and Groom Photos&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;6:00 pm \u2013 Wedding Party Introduction&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;6:15pm \u2013 Dinner starts being served; Cake cutting, Speeches&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;7:15 pm \u2013 First dance, Father\/Daughter dance, Mother\/Son dance, Kids dance, Garter\/Bouquet Toss, Shoe Game&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;8:00 pm \u2013 Dancing&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:#000000;\"&gt;11:00 pm \u2013 Reception Ends&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1882725,"PostDate":1421147937,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><span  style=\"font-size:18px\"><strong>Update 1.13.2015<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I am working on printables today, and here are a few templates.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Wedding Day Timeline Card<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The wedding day timeline I pretty much straight up used someone elses on here (I can't find her thread right now, whoops) and just changed the times\/what it said. \u00a0I'm planning on changing the fonts on my personal computer (I can't download fonts to my work computer). I'm planning on printing these via Vistaprint on the regular or 4x6 postcards. \u00a0Probably will include our instagram tag & wedding day photo site information on the back (is it worth $5 to print? probably, then I don't have to do it elsewhere like business cards...). \u00a0These are going in the OOT bags.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79711-wedding-guest-timeline\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_56606.png' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='wedding guest timeline'  width='200' height='150'  alt='wedding guest timeline' id='sml_image_view_79711' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><b>Menu\/Photo Scavenger Hunt<\/b><\/p>\n<p>I've also included my menu front & back with photo scavenger hunt. \u00a0I again used the words from another person for the photo scavenger hunt, although I did customize the shots to capture. \u00a0These I will print on rack cards and have places on the plates at the reception. \u00a0I think this is the menu we're going to go with; I was trying to find things that everyone would like, or at least most everyone. \u00a0Still debating, and will have FI have final say (he was verbally on board, and suggested the Chef Salad instead of Caesar as well as the Minestrone soup, and agreed on the reasons behind the dessert being a brownie & ice cream, especially with cake already!)<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79712-menu-front\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_131866.png' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='menu front'  width='91' height='200'  alt='menu front' id='sml_image_view_79712' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/79713-photo-scavenger-hunt-back\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_21345.png' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='photo scavenger hunt back'  width='92' height='200'  alt='photo scavenger hunt back' id='sml_image_view_79713' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm working through my wedding day timeline, and deciding if I want to go with Styling Trio for my hair\/makeup or the salon. \u00a0I requested a quote, and got a bunch of social media information (which I had already found!) but no pricing. \u00a0The salon pricing isn't terrible - it's $50\/bridesmaid & $220ish for me for hair\/hair trial\/makeup (if I pay up front). \u00a0I don't have any examples of their work though, and that worries me...I am considering doing a mixture of both salon & styling trio. \u00a0Or all of one\/the other. \u00a0I need them to respond with pricing though, haha!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Does this seem a reasonable timeline for a 4pm wedding? \u00a0I have Samuel Luna from 230-830pm (photographer).<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">9:00 am \u2013 Nails<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">11:00 am \u2013 Room Service Lunch (ladies)<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">12:00 pm \u2013 Hair & Makeup<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">2:30 pm - Photos of Groom and Groomsman getting ready<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">3:00 pm - Photos of Bride and Bridesmaids getting ready<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">3:45 pm - Guests arrive at wedding ceremony site<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">4:00 pm - Wedding Ceremony<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">4:30 pm - Tequila Shot Toast<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">4:45 pm \u2013 Group Photos<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">5:00 pm - Family Photos and Informal Cocktail Hour (Lobby Bar)<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">5:15 pm - Bride and Groom Photos<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">6:00 pm \u2013 Wedding Party Introduction<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">6:15pm \u2013 Dinner starts being served; Cake cutting, Speeches<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">7:15 pm \u2013 First dance, Father\/Daughter dance, Mother\/Son dance, Kids dance, Garter\/Bouquet Toss, Shoe Game<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">8:00 pm \u2013 Dancing<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:#000000\">11:00 pm \u2013 Reception Ends<\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"32 guests, Bride & Groom & 2 kids booked!Planning Thread - lots of pictures, DIY\/templates and ongoing updates!<br><br><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/<\/span><\/a>","Email":"marinarhianne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.149.51.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1387570652,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275696.jpeg?_r=1426773379","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"marinah84","Id":275696,"Name":"marinah84","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"198.163.47.9","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"84720e5aba7a07bec02dfa47d84ca1bd","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"marinah84\"] everything looks amazing! &amp;nbsp;Your attention to detail is incredible. &amp;nbsp;And I LOVE the boudoir book. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m totally planning on making one for my fella as a wedding gift.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Question for you: did you print the invites yourself?&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1882737,"PostDate":1421160184,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"275696\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/275696-marinah84\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">marinah84<\/span><\/a> everything looks amazing! \u00a0Your attention to detail is incredible. \u00a0And I LOVE the boudoir book. \u00a0I'm totally planning on making one for my fella as a wedding gift.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Question for you: did you print the invites yourself?\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"slfehr@outlook.com","IpAddress":"24.114.26.10","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1420208577,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"pykx82","Id":281560,"Name":"pykx82","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"216.200.128.254","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"9ecdac9ad50f3c4acd8d0d78019dcf96","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"pykx82\"] Thanks!! &amp;nbsp;It&#039;s a blast, I&#039;d totally recommend it!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We did print them out ourselves. &amp;nbsp;I got paper online, and printed some on both our inkjet home printer and some on my FI&#039;s work laserjet. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;d recommend printing on a laserjet - the paper seemed to absorb the inkjet ink more, if that makes sense? &amp;nbsp;They were just more muted\/not as crisp looking.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;It was pretty easy, as I used the Aylee Bits template and a jacket template I found on here. &amp;nbsp;So it was just customizing it, and cutting them out\/folding the jackets. &amp;nbsp;They took a bit of time to put together, but I loved them!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For anyone looking to do a boudoir book,and you&#039;re in the Chicagoland area, this is our family friend\/photographer who does them. &amp;nbsp;She does an amazing job, and is so sweet and it&#039;s not uncomfortable at all: &amp;nbsp;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/AmandaBrownPhotography1&#039;&gt;https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/AmandaBrownPhotography1&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1882741,"PostDate":1421160937,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281560\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281560-pykx82\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">pykx82<\/span><\/a> Thanks!! \u00a0It's a blast, I'd totally recommend it!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We did print them out ourselves. \u00a0I got paper online, and printed some on both our inkjet home printer and some on my FI's work laserjet. \u00a0I'd recommend printing on a laserjet - the paper seemed to absorb the inkjet ink more, if that makes sense? \u00a0They were just more muted\/not as crisp looking.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It was pretty easy, as I used the Aylee Bits template and a jacket template I found on here. \u00a0So it was just customizing it, and cutting them out\/folding the jackets. \u00a0They took a bit of time to put together, but I loved them!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>For anyone looking to do a boudoir book,and you're in the Chicagoland area, this is our family friend\/photographer who does them. \u00a0She does an amazing job, and is so sweet and it's not uncomfortable at all: \u00a0<a href='https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/AmandaBrownPhotography1' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>https:\/\/www.facebook...ownPhotography1<\/a><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"32 guests, Bride & Groom & 2 kids booked!Planning Thread - lots of pictures, DIY\/templates and ongoing updates!<br><br><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/<\/span><\/a>","Email":"marinarhianne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.149.51.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1387570652,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275696.jpeg?_r=1426773379","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"marinah84","Id":275696,"Name":"marinah84","IsOnline":true}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":254,"TotalPages":26,"CurrentPage":80,"NextPage":90,"PreviousPage":70,"LastPage":250},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
