{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8c4961398f8c9335a62943c1ca977af4","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hahah, well he&#039;s going to have a nice surprise when he sees all the suitcases :P&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I just followed your page on facebook! I really need to try these things :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1887895,"PostDate":1425229226,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hahah, well he's going to have a nice surprise when he sees all the suitcases <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I just followed your page on facebook! I really need to try these things <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359748704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.32.161.137","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e823d277f8f6f603b783762cbe046ec5","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;We&#039;re going to need to buy a few more big ones, I think :) &amp;nbsp;We get 6 free checked bags, it&#039;d be a waste to check little ones if it means we&#039;ll need to pay for bags! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1887898,"PostDate":1425230453,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>We're going to need to buy a few more big ones, I think <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0We get 6 free checked bags, it'd be a waste to check little ones if it means we'll need to pay for bags! \u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"32 guests, Bride & Groom & 2 kids booked!Planning Thread - lots of pictures, DIY\/templates and ongoing updates!<br><br><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/<\/span><\/a>","Email":"marinarhianne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.149.51.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1387570652,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275696.jpeg?_r=1426773379","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"marinah84","Id":275696,"Name":"marinah84","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"9461783a55b945788790c1bb8cb0adbf","RawContent":"[quote name=\"marinah84\" post=\"1887898\" timestamp=\"1425244853\"]\nWe&#039;re going to need to buy a few more big ones, I think :)  We get 6 free checked bags, it&#039;d be a waste to check little ones if it means we&#039;ll need to pay for bags![\/quote]you&#039;re lucky! we don&#039;t get more than the regular, and even then, now we need to pay for the first bag for some airlines. I haven&#039;t quite checked the rules on that yet. \n\nI was hoping that I didn&#039;t have to bring a lot but things are starting to add up for sure. I tend overpack like it&#039;s no one&#039;s business, for any trip, so I can&#039;t even imagine what it&#039;s going to be like this time around.","Attachments":[],"Id":1887900,"PostDate":1425232155,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>marinah84, on 01 March 2015 - 05:20 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>We're going to need to buy a few more big ones, I think <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0We get 6 free checked bags, it'd be a waste to check little ones if it means we'll need to pay for bags! \u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>you're lucky! we don't get more than the regular, and even then, now we need to pay for the first bag for some airlines. I haven't quite checked the rules on that yet.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I was hoping that I didn't have to bring a lot but things are starting to add up for sure. I tend overpack like it's no one's business, for any trip, so I can't even imagine what it's going to be like this time around.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359748704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"64.231.99.29","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d1c4961e27b3ecbaad4b23cb5ce4fac5","RawContent":"[quote name=\"marinah84\" post=\"1887358\" timestamp=\"1424801564\"]\n@[member=\"MrsCtoB\"] @[member=\"TinkerSofi\"]\n\nThanks!  Those are great descriptions, and sound really good.  I&#039;m guessing its the 3 leches, versus dulce de leche.  I&#039;m all about sweet, so it could be a good option!\n\n\n\n[b][size=6]HORRIBLE UPDATE:[\/size][\/b]\n[size=6][size=4]So before my workout last night, I was playing with the dog and throwing the toy.  I tripped and caught myself in a standing position, but heard a \"pop\" in my foot.  Turns out I have a fracture in my 5th metatarsal (little toe) and am in a walking shoe for probably 6 weeks.  GUESS WHAT HAPPENS IN LESS THAN 3 WEEKS?!  I&#039;m so upset :(  I&#039;m trying to be optimistic as much as possible, of course.  [\/size][\/size]\n\n[size=6][size=4]The good thing is the pain should subside in 7-10 days, and the shoe is removable so I theoretically shouldn&#039;t be too worried about it, for the wedding itself.  The Monday excursion may be an issue, and getting around the resort a lot.  I&#039;ll have to see if they have scooters and things, just in case.  I have an appointment on Friday with the surgeon, to make sure it doesn&#039;t require surgery.  Until then, I am chugging ibuprofen\/icing it and elevating it as much as possible.  Heal, heal, heal!  [\/size][\/size][\/quote]\nOh no! That definitely isn&#039;t good. You have my sympathathy for sure!! Not to worry you, but I did almost the exact thing, only 2nd metatarsal (next to big toe) and I ended up in a walking cast for 17 weeks. It should have been pinned (found this out after the fact) but it never healed properly even after being in the cast that long. We went to Mexico after the cast was off and I still couldn&#039;t do the ruins at Coba. My husband climbed but I didn&#039;t.\n\nBe very careful what you put on your feet. I know it&#039;s your baby toe but you could still affect how it heals. Yes - keep it elevated for sure and the ibuprofen will help the swelling.\n\nGood luck!! You&#039;re getting so close now. I&#039;m anxious to hear your report when you get back!!\n[quote name=\"marinah84\" post=\"1887634\" timestamp=\"1424987699\"]\n@calgarybride2015 @veryvalero @TinkerSofi @[member=\"kcole123\"] @[member=\"MrsCtoB\"] @[member=\"Meandhim\"]\n\n\nThank you so much, ladies, for all of the kind wishes!  It&#039;s starting to bruise now, and I&#039;m doing my best to stay off of it.  I&#039;m just thankful it wasn&#039;t worse!  I&#039;m already able to walk slowly so that it doesn&#039;t look too bad, so I&#039;m sure 2 more weeks will do wonders!  Found out the ortho only comes to this part of the state 2x a month, and so my appointment is the Friday before we leave, on the 6th!  If I do need surgery (which I doubt) I feel like it&#039;ll be halfway healed by then anyway haha.\n\n\n[b]Vistaprint[\/b]\n\nSo I found a MAJOR error on the programs, lol.  Not only did it say that my bridesmaid was \"friend of the groom\", it said FIEND of the groom.  FIEND.  As in DEVIL.  I about DIED laughing when I saw that!\n\nLuckily Groupon has a Vistaprint coupon right now for $27 for $70, so I went ahead and fixed the issue.  I got it printed on 1 side - it saved me $5 AND will allow me to do the fans, haha.  I&#039;ll glue them to the others already printed, with the stick in the middle.  It&#039;s what I was going to do initially, and now I can go ahead and do it.\n\nI also got the door hangers printed on rack cards - it was harder to get to $70 than I thought it would be, haha, since I just did the order for the last bit.  I used a stock image of a beach and used an extra menu rack card to hole punch to see where the hole will lay. \n\n\n\n\nI also got address labels for the thank you cards after we get back (had to get to that $70 haha).\n\n\nI also got my self a few items, to make up the balance.  I got a beach bag to carry my stuff around, and a tshirt :)\n\nBag (I got the 2-toned larger bag):\n\n\n\nShirt:\n\n\nI already got the FI a \"Game Over\" tshirt that I&#039;m giving him, so I figured I needed a wedding themed shirt as well :)\n\n\n\n[b]Sand Ceremony[\/b]\nI asked my friend to do the reading at the ceremony - this is what I have so far (probably mostly \"borrowed\" from this forum, haha):\n\n\n[i][color=#000000][font=arial][size=2]Marina and Greg,[\/size][\/font][\/color][\/i]\n[i][color=#000000][font=arial][size=2]As you stand beside the ocean, may your love always be as constant as the tide; waves flowing endlessly from the depths of the sea. Just as water is the eternal force of life, so is love. Love is the force that allows us to face fear and uncertainty with courage.\n\nYou have just sealed your relationship by the giving and receiving of rings. But although you will be sharing one life, never forget that you are two separate people. Cherish and affirm your differences. Love each other. Keep your commitment primary. Together you will laugh and cry, be sick and well, be happy and angry, share and grow.[\/size][\/font][\/color][\/i]\n\n[i][color=#000000][font=arial][size=2]We will now celebrate Marina and Greg&#039;s union with a symbolic sand ceremony. [b](Pause)[\/b][\/size][\/font][\/color][\/i]\n\n[i][color=#000000][font=arial][size=2]Marina and Greg, today you are making a lasting commitment to share the rest of your lives with each other. This commitment is symbolized through the pouring and combining of these of these individual containers of sand. Each container represents the separate journeys you once were on. [b](B&amp;amp;G take turns pouring\/layering sand[\/b]) Each of you comes to this relationship with unique strengths, vulnerabilities, and histories. As individuals, you are beautiful people all on your own. Yet when the two of you are blended together, you form something even more beautiful. Those strengths can blossom and those vulnerabilities cared for. Each one holds its own unique beauty, strength, and character. They can stand on their own and be whole, without need of anything else.[\/size][\/font][\/color][\/i]\n[i][color=#000000][font=arial][size=2]However when these two are blended together they create and entirely new and extraordinarily more intricate entity, as symbolized by the new blended colour. [b](Both B&amp;amp;G pour sand together)[\/b]\n\nAs the sand has blended together, your lives too are joined. Your once solitary journeys have become one of companionship, as you now set forth on a single path together into your future. Your friends and family are as one as well. You will now share those who are a part of your lives as you walk hand-in-hand. Just as these grains of sand can never be separated and poured again into the individual vases, so will the love and bond between the two of you render you inseparable.[\/size][\/font][\/color][\/i]\n\n\nAny suggestions on funny wording\/changes?  \n\nI have been thinking about the sand ceremony vases, also, and didn&#039;t want to have to find a nice looking funnel and bring down vases to pour and have it spill, etc.  I saw this on pinterest and it got me thinking:\n\n\n\nI have quite a few of these liquor pourers, so was looking for a bottle that would work.  I then had the brilliant idea to look at oil pourers (the things you put on your kitchen counters to pour olive oil)!  I ended up getting 2 for $6 at Walmart, and the holes are pretty big so the sand should pour great!  And if it doesn&#039;t, we can pull out the pourer and pour through the wider mouth!\n\n\n\n\n\nIf I finish everything else, I may decorate the bottles with the leftover wooden intials &amp;amp; raffia\/ribbon.  Otherwise, I&#039;m sure it&#039;s fine like this :)\n\n\n\n[b]Bridesmaid Gifts[\/b]\nSo this is one area I went WAY over the top with this wedding, my gifts to my girls.  I&#039;ve made them a little \"wedding day survival\" bag that includes some pampering items (will post pictures after I get them all packed!), in addition to the custom robe &amp;amp; other items I already got.  \n\nI added these new items I found out about in January, [b]Jamberry Nail Wraps[\/b]!  I LOVE them!  They last almost 2 weeks on my fingers (on my 4th manicure) and up to 6 weeks on the toes, go on natural or artificial nails, and come in over 300 designs!  You get at least 2 manis\/2 pedis per sheet, and I have baby toes so I actually have enough for several more pedicures\/accent nails too.\n\nFor the bridesmaids, I picked out designs to match my girl&#039;s personalities.  They don&#039;t have to wear them at the wedding, but can if they want to, especially if they don&#039;t want to pay for the nail salon.  All you need is a pair of scissors and a hair dryer to apply! I&#039;m getting artificial nails this week or early next week (depends on if I can hobble to the salon or not, haha) and will have a wrap put on there to wear until my wedding.  I will have the nail salon at the resort do a fill on my nails the morning of the wedding, and apply a french manicure wrap so it&#039;ll last 2 more weeks!\n\n\n\nThey ship in the USA and Canada right now, and if you&#039;re interested, check out the designs.  There are about 100 designs expiring on Feb 28th, and a similar number of new designs starting March 1st.  Here&#039;s my site! [url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net[\/url]   \n\nYou can also host online facebook parties, playing games &amp;amp; running specials, and earn free\/discounted wraps!  I ended up earning 7 free wraps (including 2 exclusive wraps for hosting a party), 5 half off wraps and 25% off the rest of my order, just for hosting a party for my friends on Facebook.  \n\nCan you tell I&#039;m excited about these, lol?  I&#039;m horrible at doing my nails, and this is an easy (and inexpensive) way for me to have pretty nails, even with my kiddos and working out and typing on the computer all the time!\n\n[i]Which do you think I should apply for the pre-wedding festivities?[\/i]\n\nAtlantis - I adore how this fades from blue to green, my daughter calls them \"mermaid\" nails:\n[url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/atlantis#.VO-SNPnF98E\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/atlantis#.VO-SNPnF98E[\/url]\n\n\nEverything Nice - This is one of my FAVORITES - the chevron is trendy, and it&#039;s so pretty too!\n[url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/everything-nice#.VO-TSvnF98E\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/everything-nice#.VO-TSvnF98E[\/url]\n\n\nChampagne Toast and\/or Sugar &amp;amp; Spice - I love this combo, but think they&#039;d be nice alone too.  Champagne Toast is very classy\/elegant, maybe for the ceremony?\n\n[url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/champagne-toast#.VO-T8PnF98E\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/champagne-toast#.VO-T8PnF98E[\/url]\n[url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/sugar-spice#.VO-UuPnF98E\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/sugar-spice#.VO-UuPnF98E[\/url]\n\n\n\n\nThese are the designs I got my bridesmaids - I think they&#039;ll LOVE them! :\n\nStar Crossed - MOH\n[url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/star-crossed#.VO-VFPnF98E\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/star-crossed#.VO-VFPnF98E[\/url]\n\nSeascape - my BFF\n[url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/seascape#.VO-VNPnF98E\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/seascape#.VO-VNPnF98E[\/url]\n\nTurkish Delight - good friend\n[url=\"http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/turkish-delight#.VO-VT_nF98E\"]http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/turkish-delight#.VO-VT_nF98E[\/url]\n\nNavy Quatrefoil - FI&#039;s sister\/groomsmaid\n[url=\"http:\/\/www.jamberrynails.net\/product\/navy-quatrefoil#.VO-VwPnF98E\"]http:\/\/www.jamberrynails.net\/product\/navy-quatrefoil#.VO-VwPnF98E[\/url][\/quote]\nOk. Sorry to sound like a total dork, but what are these? I looked on the site and I love some of the colours and patterns. They&#039;re totally cool. I pay to get my nails done but is this something I could do on my own?","Attachments":[],"Id":1887904,"PostDate":1425235275,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>marinah84, on 24 February 2015 - 02:12 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"266526\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/266526-mrsctob\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">MrsCtoB<\/span><\/a> @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"265511\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/265511-tinkersofi\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">TinkerSofi<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thanks! \u00a0Those are great descriptions, and sound really good. \u00a0I'm guessing its the 3 leches, versus dulce de leche. \u00a0I'm all about sweet, so it could be a good option!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><span  style=\"font-size:24px\">HORRIBLE UPDATE:<\/span><\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-size:24px\"><span  style=\"font-size:14px\">So before my workout last night, I was playing with the dog and throwing the toy. \u00a0I tripped and caught myself in a standing position, but heard a \"pop\" in my foot. \u00a0Turns out I have a fracture in my 5th metatarsal (little toe) and am in a walking shoe for probably 6 weeks. \u00a0GUESS WHAT HAPPENS IN LESS THAN 3 WEEKS?! \u00a0I'm so upset <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/> \u00a0I'm trying to be optimistic as much as possible, of course. \u00a0<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-size:24px\"><span  style=\"font-size:14px\">The good thing is the pain should subside in 7-10 days, and the shoe is removable so I theoretically shouldn't be too worried about it, for the wedding itself. \u00a0The Monday excursion may be an issue, and getting around the resort a lot. \u00a0I'll have to see if they have scooters and things, just in case. \u00a0I have an appointment on Friday with the surgeon, to make sure it doesn't require surgery. \u00a0Until then, I am chugging ibuprofen\/icing it and elevating it as much as possible. \u00a0Heal, heal, heal! \u00a0<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Oh no! That definitely isn't good. You have my sympathathy for sure!! Not to worry you, but I did almost the exact thing, only 2nd metatarsal (next to big toe) and I ended up in a walking cast for 17 weeks. It should have been pinned (found this out after the fact) but it never healed properly even after being in the cast that long. We went to Mexico after the cast was off and I still couldn't do the ruins at Coba. My husband climbed but I didn't.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Be very careful what you put on your feet. I know it's your baby toe but you could still affect how it heals. Yes - keep it elevated for sure and the ibuprofen will help the swelling.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Good luck!! You're getting so close now. I'm anxious to hear your report when you get back!!<\/p><br \/><p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>marinah84, on 26 February 2015 - 05:54 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@calgarybride2015\u00a0@veryvalero\u00a0@TinkerSofi @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277264\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277264-kcole123\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">kcole123<\/span><\/a> @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"266526\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/266526-mrsctob\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">MrsCtoB<\/span><\/a> @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"268499\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/268499-meandhim\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Meandhim<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thank you so much, ladies, for all of the kind wishes! \u00a0It's starting to bruise now, and I'm doing my best to stay off of it. \u00a0I'm just thankful it wasn't worse! \u00a0I'm already able to walk slowly so that it doesn't look too bad, so I'm sure 2 more weeks will do wonders! \u00a0Found out the ortho only comes to this part of the state 2x a month, and so my appointment is the Friday before we leave, on the 6th! \u00a0If I do need surgery (which I doubt) I feel like it'll be halfway healed by then anyway haha.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Vistaprint<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So I found a MAJOR error on the programs, lol. \u00a0Not only did it say that my bridesmaid was \"friend of the groom\", it said FIEND of the groom. \u00a0FIEND. \u00a0As in DEVIL. \u00a0I about DIED laughing when I saw that!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Luckily Groupon has a Vistaprint coupon right now for $27 for $70, so I went ahead and fixed the issue. \u00a0I got it printed on 1 side - it saved me $5 AND will allow me to do the fans, haha. \u00a0I'll glue them to the others already printed, with the stick in the middle. \u00a0It's what I was going to do initially, and now I can go ahead and do it.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I also got the door hangers printed on rack cards - it was harder to get to $70 than I thought it would be, haha, since I just did the order for the last bit. \u00a0I used a stock image of a beach and used an extra menu rack card to hole punch to see where the hole will lay.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I also got address labels for the thank you cards after we get back (had to get to that $70 haha).<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I also got my self a few items, to make up the balance. \u00a0I got a beach bag to carry my stuff around, and a tshirt <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Bag (I got the 2-toned larger bag):<\/div>\n<div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Shirt:<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I already got the FI a \"Game Over\" tshirt that I'm giving him, so I figured I needed a wedding themed shirt as well <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><strong>Sand Ceremony<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>I asked my friend to do the reading at the ceremony - this is what I have so far (probably mostly \"borrowed\" from this forum, haha):<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><em><span  style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:arial, sans-serif;color:#000000\">Marina and Greg,<\/span><\/em><\/div>\n<p><em><span  style=\"color:#000000\"><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">As you stand beside the ocean, may your love always be as constant as the tide; waves flowing endlessly from the depths of the sea. Just as water is the eternal force of life, so is love. Love is the force that allows us to face fear and uncertainty with courage.<br><br>\nYou have just sealed your relationship by the giving and receiving of rings. But although you will be sharing one life, never forget that you are two separate people. Cherish and affirm your differences. Love each other. Keep your commitment primary. Together you will laugh and cry, be sick and well, be happy and angry, share and grow.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><em><span  style=\"color:#000000\"><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">We will now celebrate\u00a0Marina and Greg's union with a symbolic sand ceremony. <strong>(Pause)<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><em><span  style=\"color:#000000\"><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Marina and Greg, today you are making a lasting commitment to share the rest of your lives with each other. This commitment is symbolized through the pouring and combining of these of these individual containers of sand. Each container represents the separate journeys you once were on. <strong>(B&G take turns pouring\/layering sand<\/strong>) Each of you comes to this relationship with unique strengths, vulnerabilities, and histories. As individuals, you are beautiful people all on your own. Yet when the two of you are blended together, you form something even more beautiful. Those strengths can blossom and those vulnerabilities cared for. Each one holds its own unique beauty, strength, and character. They can stand on their own and be whole, without need of anything else.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p>\n<p><em><span  style=\"color:#000000\"><span  style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">However when these two are blended together they create and entirely new and extraordinarily more intricate entity, as symbolized by the new blended colour. <strong>(Both B&G pour sand together)<\/strong><br><br>\nAs the sand has blended together, your lives too are joined. Your once solitary journeys have become one of companionship, as you now set forth on a single path together into your future. Your friends and family are as one as well. You will now share those who are a part of your lives as you walk hand-in-hand. Just as these grains of sand can never be separated and poured again into the individual vases, so will the love and bond between the two of you render you inseparable.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>Any suggestions on funny wording\/changes? \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I have been thinking about the sand ceremony vases, also, and didn't want to have to find a nice looking funnel and bring down vases to pour and have it spill, etc. \u00a0I saw this on pinterest and it got me thinking:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I have quite a few of these liquor pourers, so was looking for a bottle that would work. \u00a0I then had the brilliant idea to look at oil pourers (the things you put on your kitchen counters to pour olive oil)! \u00a0I ended up getting 2 for $6 at Walmart, and the holes are pretty big so the sand should pour great! \u00a0And if it doesn't, we can pull out the pourer and pour through the wider mouth!<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>If I finish everything else, I may decorate the bottles with the leftover wooden intials & raffia\/ribbon. \u00a0Otherwise, I'm sure it's fine like this <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>Bridesmaid Gifts<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>So this is one area I went WAY over the top with this wedding, my gifts to my girls. \u00a0I've made them a little \"wedding day survival\" bag that includes some pampering items (will post pictures after I get them all packed!), in addition to the custom robe & other items I already got. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I added these new items I found out about in January,\u00a0<strong>Jamberry Nail Wraps<\/strong>! \u00a0I LOVE them! \u00a0They last almost 2 weeks on my fingers (on my 4th manicure) and up to 6 weeks on the toes, go on natural or artificial nails, and come in over 300 designs! \u00a0You get at least 2 manis\/2 pedis per sheet, and I have baby toes so I actually have enough for several more pedicures\/accent nails too.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>For the bridesmaids, I picked out designs to match my girl's personalities. \u00a0They don't have to wear them at the wedding, but can if they want to, especially if they don't want to pay for the nail salon. \u00a0All you need is a pair of scissors and a hair dryer to apply! I'm getting artificial nails this week or early next week (depends on if I can hobble to the salon or not, haha) and will have a wrap put on there to wear until my wedding. \u00a0I will have the nail salon at the resort do a fill on my nails the morning of the wedding, and apply a french manicure wrap so it'll last 2 more weeks!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>They ship in the USA and Canada right now, and if you're interested, check out the designs. \u00a0There are about 100 designs expiring on Feb 28th, and a similar number of new designs starting March 1st. \u00a0Here's my site!\u00a0<a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net<\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You can also host online facebook parties, playing games & running specials, and earn free\/discounted wraps! \u00a0I ended up earning 7 free wraps (including 2 exclusive wraps for hosting a party), 5 half off wraps and 25% off the rest of my order, just for hosting a party for my friends on Facebook. \u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Can you tell I'm excited about these, lol? \u00a0I'm horrible at doing my nails, and this is an easy (and inexpensive) way for me to have pretty nails, even with my kiddos and working out and typing on the computer all the time!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><em>Which do you think I should apply for the pre-wedding festivities?<\/em><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Atlantis - I adore how this fades from blue to green, my daughter calls them \"mermaid\" nails:<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/atlantis#.VO-SNPnF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne...is#.VO-SNPnF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Everything Nice - This is one of my FAVORITES - the chevron is trendy, and it's so pretty too!<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/everything-nice#.VO-TSvnF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne...ce#.VO-TSvnF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Champagne Toast and\/or Sugar & Spice - I love this combo, but think they'd be nice alone too. \u00a0Champagne Toast is very classy\/elegant, maybe for the ceremony?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/champagne-toast#.VO-T8PnF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne...st#.VO-T8PnF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/sugar-spice#.VO-UuPnF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne...ce#.VO-UuPnF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>These are the designs I got my bridesmaids - I think they'll LOVE them! :<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Star Crossed - MOH<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/star-crossed#.VO-VFPnF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne...ed#.VO-VFPnF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Seascape - my BFF<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/seascape#.VO-VNPnF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne...pe#.VO-VNPnF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Turkish Delight - good friend<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/marinarhianne.jamberrynails.net\/product\/turkish-delight#.VO-VT_nF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/marinarhianne...ht#.VO-VT_nF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Navy Quatrefoil - FI's sister\/groomsmaid<\/p>\n<p><a href='http:\/\/www.jamberrynails.net\/product\/navy-quatrefoil#.VO-VwPnF98E' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.jamberryn...il#.VO-VwPnF98E<\/a><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Ok. Sorry to sound like a total dork, but what are these? I looked on the site and I love some of the colours and patterns. They're totally cool. I pay to get my nails done but is this something I could do on my own?<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283444599,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1426134867","PhotoWidth":668,"PhotoHeight":600,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"64.231.99.29","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3f7b3d8c1c0b827803296842d8126347","RawContent":"[quote name=\"TinkerSofi\" post=\"1887895\" timestamp=\"1425243626\"]\nHahah, well he&#039;s going to have a nice surprise when he sees all the suitcases :P\n\nI just followed your page on facebook! I really need to try these things :)[\/quote]\nMe too! But I&#039;m still not completely sure what they are! lol Sorry. I&#039;m old! That&#039;s the only excuse I have.","Attachments":[],"Id":1887908,"PostDate":1425237134,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>TinkerSofi, on 01 March 2015 - 05:00 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Hahah, well he's going to have a nice surprise when he sees all the suitcases <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I just followed your page on facebook! I really need to try these things <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Me too! But I'm still not completely sure what they are! lol Sorry. I'm old! That's the only excuse I have.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283444599,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1426134867","PhotoWidth":668,"PhotoHeight":600,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"209.91.107.220","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4d95d3b950b3ff2030c7c8cb43979c59","RawContent":"[quote name=\"acw271011\" post=\"1887908\" timestamp=\"1425251534\"]\nMe too! But I&#039;m still not completely sure what they are! lol Sorry. I&#039;m old! That&#039;s the only excuse I have.[\/quote]They&#039;re like an instant manicure haha. They are almost like stickers, so you cut them to kind of fit your nail and you blow them a little with a blow drier and voila! You have instant nail polish with all these really sweet patterns. They also last much longer than regular polish (about 2 weeks) and you don&#039;t have to wait for them to dry like regular nail polish. Also, shellac lasts pretty long, but at least for me it destroys my nails for 4 months, so it&#039;s not worth it. These things don&#039;t ruin your natural nail :) \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1887909,"PostDate":1425237451,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>acw271011, on 01 March 2015 - 07:12 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>Me too! But I'm still not completely sure what they are! lol Sorry. I'm old! That's the only excuse I have.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nThey're like an instant manicure haha. They are almost like stickers, so you cut them to kind of fit your nail and you blow them a little with a blow drier and voila! You have instant nail polish with all these really sweet patterns. They also last much longer than regular polish (about 2 weeks) and you don't have to wait for them to dry like regular nail polish. Also, shellac lasts pretty long, but at least for me it destroys my nails for 4 months, so it's not worth it. These things don't ruin your natural nail <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359748704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"44fbbf8fd75e5d68f96029d5d4d5cc8d","RawContent":"I tried jam berries recently and while it took a couple tries to figure them out I can back them up :) \n\n\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1887914,"PostDate":1425241334,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I tried jam berries recently and while it took a couple tries to figure them out I can back them up <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> <br><br><br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"64.231.99.29","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7a638957a9e46ce830b0e56983f70cda","RawContent":"[quote name=\"TinkerSofi\" post=\"1887909\" timestamp=\"1425251851\"]\nThey&#039;re like an instant manicure haha. They are almost like stickers, so you cut them to kind of fit your nail and you blow them a little with a blow drier and voila! You have instant nail polish with all these really sweet patterns. They also last much longer than regular polish (about 2 weeks) and you don&#039;t have to wait for them to dry like regular nail polish. Also, shellac lasts pretty long, but at least for me it destroys my nails for 4 months, so it&#039;s not worth it. These things don&#039;t ruin your natural nail :)\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk[\/quote]\nI do shellac and yeah, it totally ruins my nails. I do about 3 then i use Nailtiques to repair them for a couple of months and just do my own. But I hate it. I don&#039;t have the time or the patience and yes, I always end up ruining one finger! Or two. Or three.\n\nI like the sound of these. How do you get them off? If there are no chemicals and they don&#039;t ruin your nails, what keeps them on and what makes them last?","Attachments":[],"Id":1887921,"PostDate":1425242318,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>TinkerSofi, on 01 March 2015 - 07:17 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>They're like an instant manicure haha. They are almost like stickers, so you cut them to kind of fit your nail and you blow them a little with a blow drier and voila! You have instant nail polish with all these really sweet patterns. They also last much longer than regular polish (about 2 weeks) and you don't have to wait for them to dry like regular nail polish. Also, shellac lasts pretty long, but at least for me it destroys my nails for 4 months, so it's not worth it. These things don't ruin your natural nail <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I do shellac and yeah, it totally ruins my nails. I do about 3 then i use Nailtiques to repair them for a couple of months and just do my own. But I hate it. I don't have the time or the patience and yes, I always end up ruining one finger! Or two. Or three.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I like the sound of these. How do you get them off? If there are no chemicals and they don't ruin your nails, what keeps them on and what makes them last?<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283444599,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1426134867","PhotoWidth":668,"PhotoHeight":600,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1425242686,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7f3d38dfeae3cf9439fbbc781fc1f3b6","RawContent":"[quote name=\"acw271011\" post=\"1887921\" timestamp=\"1425256718\"]\nI do shellac and yeah, it totally ruins my nails. I do about 3 then i use Nailtiques to repair them for a couple of months and just do my own. But I hate it. I don&#039;t have the time or the patience and yes, I always end up ruining one finger! Or two. Or three.\n\nI like the sound of these. How do you get them off? If there are no chemicals and they don&#039;t ruin your nails, what keeps them on and what makes them last?[\/quote]Shellac doesn&#039;t ruin my nails that quickly but it does I agree.  I used gel since November and just took them off - nails are trashed. \n\nYou heat them with your blow dryer and they get flexible. Then you attach them and apply pressure. Just ensure they aren&#039;t touching skin or cuticles so a good seal can be made.  Then heat them to set.  Worked good for me. One thing I learned is you can&#039;t have any overhang at the tip of your nail or they will lift. I used a manicure scissor to trim but I think nail cutters may work better.   \n\nJust heat again to take off. \n\nMarina will have way more experience and tips than I. As I only used them once but it was way less daunting then I imagined. \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1887922,"PostDate":1425242586,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>acw271011, on 01 March 2015 - 08:38 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>\nI do shellac and yeah, it totally ruins my nails. I do about 3 then i use Nailtiques to repair them for a couple of months and just do my own. But I hate it. I don't have the time or the patience and yes, I always end up ruining one finger! Or two. Or three.<br><br>\nI like the sound of these. How do you get them off? If there are no chemicals and they don't ruin your nails, what keeps them on and what makes them last?<\/p><\/div><\/div>Shellac doesn't ruin my nails that quickly but it does I agree.  I used gel since November and just took them off - nails are trashed. <br><br>\nYou heat them with your blow dryer and they get flexible. Then you attach them and apply pressure. Just ensure they aren't touching skin or cuticles so a good seal can be made.  Then heat them to set.  Worked good for me. One thing I learned is you can't have any overhang at the tip of your nail or they will lift. I used a manicure scissor to trim but I think nail cutters may work better.   <br><br>\nJust heat again to take off. <br><br>\nMarina will have way more experience and tips than I. As I only used them once but it was way less daunting then I imagined. <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.32.161.137","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77321,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6cb33a2b8b424071ecd076bfc2c0b3db","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"acw271011\"]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;ve used both nail polish remover &amp;amp; heated coconut oil to remove, and the oil works the best! &amp;nbsp;Here&#039;s a youtube explaining it:&amp;nbsp;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=HLuEOe0m9Fs&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;What I like about the oil removal is that it moisturizes at the same time, haha! &amp;nbsp;I use those little flosser sticks to ease the separation. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here&#039;s an application video with my favorite method (\"baggie\") - my first manicure took a little bit to get a hang of cutting them, but the last few have been pretty quick! &amp;nbsp;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=gNEcYcEP0Fs&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:18px;\"&gt;Update 3.1.2015&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;I finished the groom&#039;s bout today (it&#039;s the only one that still needed to be made). &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80174]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;I also decorated the sand ceremony pourer...things. &amp;nbsp;No idea what to call them, since they aren&#039;t normal sand vases :)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;I started off with just hot gluing the initials on, but it still looked a little plain.&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80175]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;So I took the smallest spray painted starfish I had, and some leftover ribbon, and played around until i was happy. &amp;nbsp;I think it turned out pretty well!&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80176]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80177]&lt;\/div&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1887929,"PostDate":1425248444,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"232000\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/232000-acw271011\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">acw271011<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I've used both nail polish remover & heated coconut oil to remove, and the oil works the best! \u00a0Here's a youtube explaining it:\u00a0<iframe id=\"ytplayer\" class=\"EmbeddedVideo\" type=\"text\/html\" width=\"640\" height=\"390\" src=\"http:\/\/youtube.com\/embed\/HLuEOe0m9Fs?html5=1&fs=1\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen webkitallowfullscreen \/><\/iframe><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>What I like about the oil removal is that it moisturizes at the same time, haha! \u00a0I use those little flosser sticks to ease the separation. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Here's an application video with my favorite method (\"baggie\") - my first manicure took a little bit to get a hang of cutting them, but the last few have been pretty quick! \u00a0<iframe id=\"ytplayer\" class=\"EmbeddedVideo\" type=\"text\/html\" width=\"640\" height=\"390\" src=\"http:\/\/youtube.com\/embed\/gNEcYcEP0Fs?html5=1&fs=1\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen webkitallowfullscreen \/><\/iframe><\/p><br \/><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><strong><span  style=\"font-size:18px\">Update 3.1.2015<\/span><\/strong><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I finished the groom's bout today (it's the only one that still needed to be made). \u00a0<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80174-groom-bout\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_365541.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Groom Bout'  width='150' height='200'  alt='Groom Bout' id='sml_image_view_80174' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I also decorated the sand ceremony pourer...things. \u00a0No idea what to call them, since they aren't normal sand vases <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>I started off with just hot gluing the initials on, but it still looked a little plain.<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80175-sand-ceremony-plain-initials\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1218321.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Sand Ceremony Plain Initials'  width='150' height='200'  alt='Sand Ceremony Plain Initials' id='sml_image_view_80175' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>So I took the smallest spray painted starfish I had, and some leftover ribbon, and played around until i was happy. \u00a0I think it turned out pretty well!<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80176-sand-ceremony-ribbon-initials\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1242933.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Sand Ceremony Ribbon Initials'  width='150' height='200'  alt='Sand Ceremony Ribbon Initials' id='sml_image_view_80176' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80177-sand-ceremony-ribbon-initials\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17712\/sml_gallery_275696_17712_1237778.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Sand Ceremony Ribbon Initials'  width='150' height='200'  alt='Sand Ceremony Ribbon Initials' id='sml_image_view_80177' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"32 guests, Bride & Groom & 2 kids booked!Planning Thread - lots of pictures, DIY\/templates and ongoing updates!<br><br><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77321-marinah84s-planning-thread-31415-crown-paradise-club-cancun\/<\/span><\/a>","Email":"marinarhianne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.149.51.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1387570652,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275696.jpeg?_r=1426773379","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"marinah84","Id":275696,"Name":"marinah84","IsOnline":true}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":254,"TotalPages":26,"CurrentPage":160,"NextPage":170,"PreviousPage":150,"LastPage":250},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
